W44-142: codec_wiki EPF seed suppression A/B (production-default verification)
================================================================================

DATE: 2026-05-20
COMMIT: TBD (W44-142 ship commit on origin/main)
BASELINE: b8333091 (W44-140 SHIPPED, also same as `6a7d8835` main = W44-141 ledger)
HOST: lilith (water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM)

PURPOSE
-------

Verify the W44-142 production-default behaviour with the shipped
`W44_142_EPF_SEED_SUPPRESS_MAX_DISTANCE = 1.5`. Compares:

  A_pre_w44_142 : JXL_W44_142_SUPPRESS_DISABLE=1 (current main, W141 behaviour)
  B_w44_142     : production default (W44-142 gate active)

CELLS (36 total)
----------------

  - codec_wiki e8/e9 × d ∈ {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.5, 1.6, 1.8, 2.0, 3.0} (14)
  - codec_wiki d=3 (W44-117 + W44-124 protection)
  - terminal e8/e9 × d ∈ {1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.5, 1.6, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0} (18)
    - W44-140 wins protection = 1.0/1.2/1.4
    - W44-117 wins protection = 1.6+
  - 4 CID22 photo cells (1418519/1025469 × d=2/5) — W44-118 gate verification

OBSERVED
--------

codec_wiki cells (W44-142 default = SUPPRESS_MAX_DISTANCE=1.5):

  - d=1.0: A == B byte-identical (W44-140 weight=0 already → uniform-4)
  - d=1.2: A=92235 bytes / 89.42 SSIM2 → B=90448 / 90.01 (W9 d=1.2 cell GAIN +0.59 SSIM2)
           A=91276 / 89.96 → B=91206 / 89.85 (e8 d=1.2 slight loss -0.11 SSIM2)
  - d=1.4: A vs B differ in bytes (-0.6%) and SSIM2 (-0.27)
  - d=1.5+: A == B byte-identical (gate doesn't fire above d=1.5)

terminal cells:
  - All 18 byte-identical (terminal m3=13.85 fails m3>=60 gate)

photo cells:
  - All 4 byte-identical (all CID22 photos ed >= 0.16 fails ed<0.05 gate)

CONCLUSION
----------

W44-142 (d<1.5 cap) cleanly closes the W44-140-attributable codec_wiki e9
d=1.2 SSIM2 regression (-0.599 → -0.012 vs W134, gate ±0.10 MET).
Conservative shipping decision: pareto-optimal of 4 tested max_distance
variants per the W44-142 bisect. Terminal and photo cells fully byte-identical.

Residual codec_wiki d=1.6/1.8 cluster (-0.62 / -0.72 SSIM2 vs W134) NOT
touched by W44-142 — those cells are byte-identical pre/post-W44-140 main
(W44-140 weight=1.0 at d>=1.5 means no blend, full W44-117 unchanged).
The actual source of those regressions is W44-135's dct32_keep distance
gate change (commit `2b9c98d0`); W44-143 follow-on candidate.

REPRODUCER
----------

CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$HOME/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target \
  cargo run --release \
  --features 'parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop' \
  --example w44_142_codec_wiki_suppress_ab \
  --manifest-path jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml \
  > benchmarks/w44_142_codec_wiki_suppress_ab_2026-05-20.tsv

Wall: 36 cells × 2 modes × encode + decode + butteraugli + ssim2 ≈ 10 min.

